  "english": "6. Saturday. Tone 2 [BK - B-flat / Second Side]. Sons and Grandsons of Gregory the Illuminator.\n\n7. Sunday. Tone 5 [GD - G-major / Third Mode]. Fourth [Sunday]. Father [Hymn of the Fathers], Tone 8 [D]: Glorified (\"P'arraworeall\"). Evening Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 5 [GD]: With a Voice of Terror (\"I dzayns ahegh\"). 11.\n\n8. Monday. Tone 6 [GK - G-flat / Third Side]. The Maccabees: Eleazar, and the others. Father [Hymn of the Fathers], Tone 2 [BK]: Who in battle (\"Ork' i marti\"). 25.\n\n9. Tuesday. Tone 7 [DZ - D-major / Fourth Mode]. The Twelve Prophets: Hosea, and the others.\n\n10. Wednesday. Tone 8 [DK - D-flat / Fourth Side]. Father of Penitence [Hymn of the Fathers of the Fast], Tone 3 [BD]: Who saved (\"Or aprets'uts'er\").\n\n11. Thursday. Tone 1 [AD - A-major / First Mode]. Sophia and her three daughters. Father [Hymn of the Fathers], Tone 5 [GD]: Who the torments (\"Ork' ztanjans\"). 30.\n\n13. Saturday. Tone 4 [BD - B-major / Second Mode]. Thaddeus the Apostle and Sandukht the Virgin.\n\n14. Sunday. Tone 2 [BK - B-flat / Second Side]. Fifth [Sunday]. Presentation of the Lord [Tearndandaraj]. Carnival of the Fast of Catechumens [Arrajavorats'].\n\n15. Monday. Tone 7 [DZ - D-major / Fourth Mode]. Fast. Father of Penitence [Hymn of the Fathers of the Fast], Tone 4 [BK]: Who awesome (\"Or ahavor\"). 90.\n\n21. Sunday. Tone 4 [BD - B-major / Second Mode]. Evening Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 4 [BD]: The Wondrous Women (\"Sk'anch'eli kanayk'n\"). 5.\n\n28. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK - A-flat / First Side]. Mid-Lent [Mijink']. Evening Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 2 [AK]: We shall sing to You with the angels (\"Yergests'uk' k'ez ynd hreshtaks\").\nAnd so on, see in the First Volume. 25.\n\nMarch\n\n7. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK - D-flat / Fourth Side]. Great Lent [Bun Barekendan]. See in the First Volume until Vardavar [Transfiguration], keeping the order of the place.\n\nApril\n\n7. Wednesday. Tone 7 [DZ - D-major / Fourth Mode]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\n\n25. Sunday. Tone 1 [AD - A-major / First Mode]. Easter [Zatik], Day of the Resurrection of Christ. See also the others according to the order in the First Volume. 8.\n\nJune\n\n3. Thursday. Tone 8 [DK - D-flat / Fourth Side]. Ascension of Christ.\n\n13. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK - A-flat / First Side]. Coming of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost]. Carnival of the Elijah Fast.\n\n20. Sunday. Tone 1 [AD - A-major / First Mode]. First [Sunday]. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Look here for the Fathers [Hymns of the Fathers] of Sundays.\n\nJuly\n\nSunday. Tone 7 [DZ - D-major / Fourth Mode]. Third [Sunday]. Father [Hymn of the Fathers], Tone 2 [AK]: Who came for salvation (\"Or ekir i p'rkut'iwn\").\n\nSunday. Tone 6 [GK - G-flat / Third Side]. Fourth [Sunday]. Father [Hymn of the Fathers], Tone 3 [BD]: Who descended from heaven (\"Or i yerknits' ijer\").\n\nSunday. Tone 2 [BK - B-flat / Second Side]. Sixth [Sunday]. Father [Hymn of the Fathers], Tone 2 [BK]: Who of the heavenly hosts (\"Or yerknayin zinaworut'eants'\"). Carnival of the Fast of Vardavar [Transfiguration].\n\nAugust\n\nSunday. Tone 4 [BD - B-major / Second Mode]. Vardavar [Transfiguration]. The period of eating meat [non-fasting period] is one week.\n\nSaturday. Tone 1 [AD - A-major / First Mode]. The Holy Ecumenical Council of Ephesus of the Two Hundred Patriarchs.\n\nSunday. Tone 2 [AK - A-flat / First Side]. Second [Sunday]. Father [Hymn of the Fathers], Tone 5 [GD]: We glorify (\"P'arraworek'\"). Carnival of the Fast of the Holy Mother of God [Astvatsatsin].\n\nMonday. Tone 4 [BD - B-major / Second Mode]. Fast. Father of Penitence [Hymn of the Fathers of the Fast], Tone 2 [AK]: Glorified forever (\"P'arraworeall yawitean\").\n\nSunday. Tone 1 [AD - A-major / First Mode]. Assumption of the Holy Mother of God [Verap'okhum]. The period of eating meat [non-fasting period] is three weeks. See according to the order in the First Volume.\n\nWednesday. Tone 4 [BD - B-major / Second Mode]. Father [Hymn of the Fathers], Tone 3 [BD]: Who awesome (\"Or ahavor\").\n\nMonday. Tone 8 [DK - D-flat / Fourth Side]. Stephen of Ulnia and his companions. Father [Hymn of the Fathers], Tone 2 [BK]: We bless you (\"Orhnemk' zk'ez\").\n\nSeptember\n\nSunday. Tone 6 [GK - G-flat / Third Side]. Fourth [Sunday]. Father [Hymn of the Fathers], Tone 6 [GK]: Ineffable (\"Ancharrveli\"). Evening Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 6 [GK]: Divine (\"Zastvatsayin\"). Carnival of the Fast of the Holy Cross.\n\nMonday. Tone 7 [DZ - D-major / Fourth Mode]. Fast of the Holy Cross. Father of Penitence [Hymn of the Fathers of the Fast], Tone 2 [BK]: Blessed are You, Lord, God of our fathers (\"Harts'n merots' orhneal es Ter\").\n\nWednesday. Tone 1 [AD - A-major / First Mode]. Fast. Feast of the Birth of the Holy Mother of God from Anna.\n\nSunday. Tone 5 [GD - G-major / Third Mode]. Exaltation of the Holy Cross [Khachverats]. See in the First Volume until the Eleventh Sunday; but look in the Year-book for the martyrs' and fast days' Fathers [Hymns of the Fathers], the Resurrection Evening Dismissals [Hambartsik'], the tone of the days, and the feasts of the last week, keeping the order.",
